================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE
================================================================================

The MIT licence above is not the whole story, because this repository is a fan
project about somebody else's work. Read it as covering three things and
excluding a fourth.

1. IT COVERS THE CODE.
   Everything under src/, tools/, scripts/, harness/, verification/ and the
   build configuration. This is original work written for this project.

2. IT COVERS THE ASSETS THIS PROJECT GENERATES.
   Every character and monster mesh, every character texture atlas, the two
   procedural materials, the city layout data and all synthesised audio are
   produced by code in this repository and are released under the same terms.

   Two of those — the procedural materials `mat.glass.window` and
   `mat.road.markings` — are additionally dedicated to the public domain under
   CC0-1.0 in tools/manifest/textures.json. That is a broader grant than this
   one, not a narrower or conflicting one, and it stands.

3. IT DOES NOT NEED TO COVER THE DOWNLOADED ASSETS, AND DOES NOT.
   The materials, models and HDRI environments fetched by `npm run assets` come
   from Poly Haven under CC0-1.0 — their authors have already dedicated them to
   the public domain. They keep that status; nothing here restricts it. Every
   one of them is credited by name in ATTRIBUTION.md anyway.

4. IT DOES NOT COVER — AND CANNOT GRANT ANY RIGHT IN — ONE PUNCH MAN.
   One Punch Man is created by ONE, illustrated by Yusuke Murata and published
   by Shueisha; the anime is produced by Madhouse and J.C.Staff. They own it.
   This project is unaffiliated with all of them, is not endorsed or approved
   by any of them, and is not for sale.

   No copyrighted One Punch Man material is included in this repository: no
   artwork, no models, no audio, no music, no fonts, no logos, no screen
   captures, no text from the manga or anime. Character names and the
   hero-ranking premise are used referentially. Every asset that depicts a
   character is original geometry this repository generates, which
   ATTRIBUTION.md verifies mechanically rather than merely asserting.

   Permission under the MIT licence to "use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
   distribute, sublicense, and/or sell" is granted by the copyright holders of
   THIS software over THIS software. It is not, and could not be, permission to
   do any of those things with One Punch Man. Anyone redistributing this
   project remains responsible for their own use of those names.
